A major gripe with Nethack 3.1; I've now managed to develop several
*very* powerful characters only to have them bludgeoned to death due to
the 'you cannot move a handspan!' blight. For example, my trusty blessed
rustproof +5 Vorpal Blade had just cloven the heads of a dozen Mordor
Orcs with one blow apiece. Cosworth The Wizard then takes a step onto the
corpses and manages to pick up the dozens and dozens of items left on the
floor...then he's told he cannot move with that burden and *POW* up
strolls one last orc who proceeds to decimate his 110(110) HP down to
zero - I didn't have time to even drop all the items I had picked up and
I couldn't even fight back!

I accept that there are more altars, more artifacts and more 'quick
benefits' in 3.1 but this kind of thing (AND those bloody invisible
bloody gnomes with their bloody invisible wands of bloody invisible
fire!) make portions of the game almost unplayable. The scope of the game
is excellent and the new additions are terrific, but I am still
disappointed.

A balanced game is not one that balances betwen such two excessive
extremes.

